  "record": {
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The maximized strip still had pywebview's native drag-region marker, so Windows treated a drag as restore-and-move even though the resize handles were disabled. Maximized state now removes that marker, and the host also rejects direct move and resize requests. The hidden real WebView2 test kept the maximized bounds unchanged, then restored normal dragging and all eight resize directions. Restart Lexeditor, maximize it, and drag the top strip; it should remain fixed.",
